<!--meta {"lead": "Fact tiles answer the questions people ask before they book: how long, how much, how long it lasts. One number, one label, side by side.", "description": "The fact tile and fact grid from style and braider pages, plus the larger stat with a delta.", "pills": ["Tabular numbers", "Status: stable"], "variants": "fact tile in a fact grid; stat with label, value and delta", "states": "default, loading, not listed (omitted), long value", "sources": ["pages/style-detail/default", "pages/braider-profile/default", "pages/style-detail/loading"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use a <b>fact tile</b> for a short, comparable figure that helps a decision: "4–7 hours · Typical time", "$160–$300 · Typical price", "From $180 · Knotless braids". Group two to four in a <code>.fact-grid</code>. Use a <b>stat</b> (large value, label, optional delta) for summaries with a trend, such as a braider's requests this month. Use a <a href="description-list.html">description list</a> when the labels matter more than the values or there are more than four facts.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Fact tile</b>: value first (h4 role), label beneath (muted, small), on a subtle background.</li>
    <li><b>Stat</b>: label first, then a large value in the h2 role, then an optional delta with arrow, sign, colour and words.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">4–7 hours</span><span class="fact__label">Typical time</span></div>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 34%; top: 30%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 34%; top: 58%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 66%; top: 74%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Value</b><small>h4 role (16px semibold), tabular figures; an en dash for ranges.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Label</b><small>Body small, muted; what the number measures.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Tile</b><small><code>--color-bg-subtle</code>, <code>--radius-md</code>, 12px padding; tiles share a grid with 16px gaps.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack]Fact grid from the knotless braids page: tiles fill the row and wrap at 8rem each.}}
<div class="fact-grid">
  <div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">4–7 hours</span><span class="fact__label">Typical time</span></div>
  <div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">$160–$300</span><span class="fact__label">Typical price</span></div>
  <div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">4–8 weeks</span><span class="fact__label">Typical wear</span></div>
</div>
  {{/example}}
  {{example:[stack]On Nia's profile: her starting price and usual duration.}}
<div class="fact-grid">
  <div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">From $180</span><span class="fact__label">Knotless braids</span></div>
  <div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">5 hours</span><span class="fact__label">Typical duration</span></div>
</div>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Stat with delta</h3>
  {{example:Delta = <code>arrow-up</code> or <code>arrow-down</code> icon + sign + colour + words; colour and arrow are never the only cue. Up means better, down worse, whatever the number did.}}
<div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Requests this month</span><span class="stat__value">24</span><span class="stat__delta stat__delta--up">{{icon:arrow-up|icon--sm}}+6 from September</span></div>
<div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Average reply time</span><span class="stat__value">3 h</span><span class="stat__delta stat__delta--down">{{icon:arrow-down|icon--sm}}1 h slower than September</span></div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="One size each: the fact tile uses the h4 role, the stat the h2 role. Use the stat when a value needs more presence."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>Facts are read-only and not focusable, so they have no hover, focus, active or disabled state. They change with the data:</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Variant</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Loading</th><th scope="col">Not listed / zero</th><th scope="col">Long value</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Fact tile</th><td><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">$160–$300</span><span class="fact__label">Typical price</span></div></td><td><div class="fact" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fact__value"><span class="skeleton skeleton--text"></span></span><span class="fact__label"><span class="skeleton skeleton--text"></span></span></div></td><td><div class="fact-grid" style="margin: 0;"><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">4–7 hours</span><span class="fact__label">Typical time</span></div><div class="fact" hidden></div></div></td><td><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">From $1,240</span><span class="fact__label">Waist-length knotless, extra small</span></div></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Stat</th><td><div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Requests</span><span class="stat__value">24</span></div></td><td><div class="stat" aria-hidden="true"><span class="stat__label"><span class="skeleton skeleton--text"></span></span><span class="stat__value"><span class="skeleton skeleton--text"></span></span></div></td><td><div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Requests</span><span class="stat__value">0</span><span class="stat__delta">No requests yet</span></div></td><td><div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Reviews</span><span class="stat__value">1,284</span></div></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<div class="fact-grid" style="margin: 0;"><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">4–7 hours</span><span class="fact__label">Typical time</span></div><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">$160–$300</span><span class="fact__label">Typical price</span></div></div><div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Requests this month</span><span class="stat__value">24</span><span class="stat__delta stat__delta--up">{{icon:arrow-up|icon--sm}}+6 from September</span></div>{{/themes}}
  <ul>
    <li><b>Loading</b>: one skeleton bar sits inside each of the value and label line boxes, so the loading tile is exactly as tall as the loaded one (70px) and nothing below moves when facts arrive; the bar's shimmer runs lighter than the tile's own fill. The tile is <code>aria-hidden</code> and the grid sets <code>aria-busy="true"</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Not listed</b>: a fact the style or braider has not published is left out (<code>hidden</code>), and the other tiles fill the row. Never a dash, "N/A" or stand-in copy. A stat's zero is a value ("0").</li>
    <li><b>Long value</b>: the value wraps inside its tile; tiles in the same row stretch to equal height.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The grid is <code>repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(8rem, 100%), 1fr))</code>: two tiles per row at 360px inside a card, three or four on wider cards, and one column when enlarged text makes 8rem wider than the grid. No breakpoints needed.</li>
    <li>Values and labels break inside their tile (<code>overflow-wrap: anywhere</code>); tiles in a row stretch to equal height.</li>
    <li>Values never truncate; they wrap. Keep them under about 12 characters so they stay on one line at 360px.</li>
    <li>A stat's value keeps the h2 role, 36px at every width.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>The tile reads <code>--color-bg-subtle</code> for its fill, <code>--color-fg-default</code> for the value and <code>--color-fg-muted</code> for the label; deltas read <code>--color-success-fg</code> and <code>--color-danger-fg</code>. In dark mode the tile becomes grey-800 on a grey-900 card, so it still reads as inset.</p>
  <p>On a sunken <code>.well</code> the tile uses <code>--color-bg-surface</code> instead (<code>.well .fact</code> in the stylesheet). In forced colours the fill disappears, so each tile gains a <code>CanvasText</code> hairline border.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>Plain elements; no ARIA pattern. Reading order is value then label ("4–7 hours, Typical time"), which makes sense spoken. Do not use <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code> for the value; the weight is visual, not importance.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Skips facts and stats; they are not interactive.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>None.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>Ranges use an en dash, which most screen readers read as "to". Arrows in deltas are <code>aria-hidden</code>; the words carry direction ("+6 from September", "1 h slower").</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Value on tile|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-subtle|4.5}}
    {{pair:Label on tile|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-subtle|4.5}}
    {{pair:Positive delta on card|--color-success-fg|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Negative delta on card|--color-danger-fg|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>Values do not count up or animate. Skeletons pause under reduced motion.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Not a target.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Value: number plus unit, short: "4–7 hours", "$160–$300", "From $180". En dash for ranges, no spaces around it.</li>
    <li>Label: what it measures, sentence case: "Typical time", "Typical price", "Typical wear".</li>
    <li>Say "typical" or "from" for estimates; the braider confirms the final price.</li>
    <li>Whole-dollar prices have no decimals: "$180", not "$180.00".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">$160–$300</span><span class="fact__label">Typical price</span></div></div><figcaption>A range with an en dash and a label that says it is typical.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">$160 - $300</span><span class="fact__label">Price</span></div></div><figcaption>A spaced hyphen and an unqualified "Price" read as a quote the braider has not given.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><div class="fact-grid" style="margin: 0;"><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">4–7 hours</span><span class="fact__label">Typical time</span></div><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">$160–$300</span><span class="fact__label">Typical price</span></div></div></div><figcaption>Leave out a fact that is not published; the other tiles fill the row.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="fact"><span class="fact__value">N/A</span><span class="fact__label">Typical wear</span></div></div><figcaption>Fill a missing fact with "N/A", a lone dash or stand-in copy such as "Ask Nia"; it invents a value.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Tile background|--color-bg-subtle}}
      {{tok:Value|--color-fg-default}}
      {{tok:Label|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Delta up / down|--color-success-fg|--color-danger-fg}}
      {{tok:Value font, fact / stat|--text-h4|--text-h2}}
      {{tok:Label font, fact / stat|--text-body-sm|--text-label}}
      {{tok:Tile padding / grid gap|--space-3|--space-4}}
      {{tok:Shape|--radius-md}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;div class="fact-grid"&gt;
  &lt;div class="fact"&gt;&lt;span class="fact__value"&gt;4–7 hours&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="fact__label"&gt;Typical time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="fact"&gt;&lt;span class="fact__value"&gt;$160–$300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="fact__label"&gt;Typical price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="stat"&gt;
  &lt;span class="stat__label"&gt;Requests this month&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="stat__value"&gt;24&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="stat__delta stat__delta--up"&gt;&lt;svg class="icon icon--sm" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"&gt;&lt;path d="M12 19V5M6 11l6-6 6 6"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;+6 from September&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.fact-grid</code></td><td>Auto-fit grid of tiles, 8rem minimum, 16px gap, 24px block margin.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.fact</code>, <code>.fact__value</code>, <code>.fact__label</code></td><td>Tile, value, label. The first mocks' unclassed <code>.fact-grid &gt; div &gt; strong/span</code> markup is still matched inside <code>:where()</code>, at zero specificity, so it never outranks the part classes.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.stat</code>, <code>.stat__label</code>, <code>.stat__value</code></td><td>Large stat.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.stat__delta--up</code> <code>.stat__delta--down</code></td><td>Delta colour; add the <code>arrow-up</code> or <code>arrow-down</code> icon (<code>.icon--sm</code>) and words.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>hidden</code> on <code>.fact</code></td><td>Omits a fact that is not published.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-busy="true"</code> on the container</td><td>While skeleton tiles show.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Extracted from these mocks:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-detail/default|typical time, price and wear}}
    {{mock:pages/braider-profile/default|starting price and duration}}
    {{mock:pages/style-detail/loading|skeleton cards with three rect fact tiles}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: values used <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code> for visual weight (system: <code>.fact__value</code>, no emphasis semantics); tiles had no class of their own (system adds <code>.fact</code> and keeps the old selectors working); a missing fact had no defined behaviour (system: the tile is omitted); the parity selectors outranked <code>.fact__value</code> and painted values as labels (now zero specificity); the loading tile was 10px taller than the loaded one (now bars inside the line boxes); tiles overflowed the card at 200% text (now <code>min(8rem, 100%)</code>); the stat with delta was added from the core set.</p>
</section>
